#. type: Title =
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-mv.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "git-mv(1)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-mv.txt:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "NAME"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-mv.txt:7
msgid "git-mv - Move or rename a file, a directory, or a symlink"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-mv.txt:10
#, no-wrap
msgid "SYNOPSIS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-mv.txt:13
msgid "'git mv' [<options>] <source>... <destination>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-mv.txt:15
#, no-wrap
msgid "DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-mv.txt:17
msgid "Move or rename a file, directory, or symlink."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-mv.txt:20
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" git mv [-v] [-f] [-n] [-k] <source> <destination>\n"
" git mv [-v] [-f] [-n] [-k] <source> ... <destination-directory>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-mv.txt:25
msgid ""
"In the first form, it renames <source>, which must exist and be either a "
"file, symlink or directory, to <destination>.  In the second form, the last "
"argument has to be an existing directory; the given sources will be moved "
"into this directory."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-mv.txt:28
msgid ""
"The index is updated after successful completion, but the change must still "
"be committed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-mv.txt:30
#, no-wrap
msgid "OPTIONS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-mv.txt:42
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`-f::`\n"
"`--force::`\n"
"\tForce renaming or moving of a file even if the <destination> exists.\n"
"`-k::`\n"
"\tSkip move or rename actions which would lead to an error\n"
"\tcondition. An error happens when a source is neither existing nor\n"
"\tcontrolled by Git, or when it would overwrite an existing\n"
"\tfile unless `-f` is given.\n"
"`-n::`\n"
"`--dry-run::`\n"
"\tDo nothing; only show what would happen\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-mv.txt:46
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`-v::`\n"
"`--verbose::`\n"
"\tReport the names of files as they are moved.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-mv.txt:48
#, no-wrap
msgid "SUBMODULES"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-mv.txt:54
msgid ""
"Moving a submodule using a gitfile (which means they were cloned with a Git "
"version 1.7.8 or newer) will update the gitfile and core.worktree setting to "
"make the submodule work in the new location.  It also will attempt to update "
"the submodule.<name>.path setting in the linkgit:gitmodules[5] file and "
"stage that file (unless -n is used)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-mv.txt:56
#, no-wrap
msgid "BUGS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-mv.txt:66
msgid ""
"Each time a superproject update moves a populated submodule (e.g. when "
"switching between commits before and after the move) a stale submodule "
"checkout will remain in the old location and an empty directory will appear "
"in the new location. To populate the submodule again in the new location the "
"user will have to run \"git submodule update\" afterwards. Removing the old "
"directory is only safe when it uses a gitfile, as otherwise the history of "
"the submodule will be deleted too. Both steps will be obsolete when "
"recursive submodule update has been implemented."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-mv.txt:68
#, no-wrap
msgid "GIT"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-mv.txt:69
msgid "Part of the linkgit:git[1] suite"
msgstr ""
